From: HobbyOS H3-winefix
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Handle SIGQUIT in a thread that has no syscall frame yet.

On x86_64 a new thread's ntdll_thread_data.syscall_frame stays NULL until
signal_start_thread() sets it up, after server_init_thread().  The server
knows the thread's unix tid as soon as it has processed init_thread, so a
process termination in that window SIGQUITs the thread while it waits for
the init_thread reply.  quit_handler() then sees is_inside_syscall() fail
(sp <= NULL is false) and calls user_mode_abort_thread( 0, NULL ), which
reads NULL+0xa8 (frame->syscall_cfa) -> SIGSEGV.  Treat a thread with no
frame as inside a syscall: abort_thread() directly.
Seen on HobbyOS as "memory fault VA=0xA8 PC=user_mode_abort_thread"
(tools/cp/p5/run-quitrace.sh proc mode, docs/cp-winefix.md).

Applies to wine-11.0 (dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c), after 0001.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -2609,7 +2609,12 @@
 {
     ucontext_t *ucontext = init_handler( sigcontext );
 
-    if (!is_inside_syscall( RSP_sig(ucontext) )) user_mode_abort_thread( 0, get_syscall_frame() );
+    /* A new thread has no syscall frame until signal_start_thread() sets it up,
+     * but the server can already SIGQUIT it while it waits for the init_thread
+     * reply: it is still in its unix-side start, so treat it as inside a syscall
+     * instead of passing a NULL frame to user_mode_abort_thread(). */
+    if (get_syscall_frame() && !is_inside_syscall( RSP_sig(ucontext) ))
+        user_mode_abort_thread( 0, get_syscall_frame() );
     abort_thread( 0 );
 }
 
